# Hebrew range "to" boundary -- the term / upper limit of a bounded interval,
# correlative of "from" (מ־) in "מ... עד...".  In the "from...to" range framing
# the upper bound is realized by עד ("until/up to"), a free word, NOT the
# proclitic ל־ (which is directional "to <place>"); "מ... עד..." is the
# temporal-range idiom.
# "עד" (ʿad): L. Glinert, *The Grammar of Modern Hebrew*, §9.2 -- עד "until, up
#   to", the terminal correlative of מ־ in temporal ranges ("מיום ראשון עד יום
#   שישי").  Academy of the Hebrew Language, s.v. עד.
עד
